The code is vulnerable to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks as it directly inserts the location hash into the HTML. The fix is to properly sanitize the input or use a safe context for the location hash. 

A safer alternative could be:
```
var safeElement = document.createElement('div');
safeElement.innerHTML = location.hash.slice(1);
element.appendChild(safeElement.childNodes[0]);
```
This code creates a new temporary element, sanitizes the input, and then appends the sanitized content to the original element.
